# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows as well as macOS and Linux. Git's
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout, which silently breaks anything that has to stay LF:
#
#   - `containers/docker-entrypoint.sh` is COPYied into the image and run as
#     `/bin/bash <script>`; a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an
#     interpreter named `/bin/bash\r` and the container dies at startup with
#     "exec ... no such file or directory", pointing at a file that plainly
#     exists.
#   - Shell scripts mounted or executed in the sandbox fail the same way.
#
# Force LF for every file the runtime, the shell, or a container executes.
# Everything else keeps git's platform default.

* text=auto

*.sh              text eol=lf
*.bash            text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
*.dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

*.py              text eol=lf
*.jinja           text eol=lf
*.md              text eol=lf
*.toml            text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.json            text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF so cmd.exe can run them.
*.bat             text eol=crlf
*.cmd             text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never touch.
*.png             binary
*.jpg             binary
*.jpeg            binary
*.gif             binary
*.ico             binary
*.pdf             binary
*.zip             binary
*.tar             binary
*.gz              binary
*.whl             binary
*.pyc             binary
